 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.54a.6",
   "daf": "54a",
   "sentenceId": 5,
   "he": "וְהָעִזִּים יוֹצְאוֹת צְרוּרוֹת. אִיתְּמַר, רַב אָמַר: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה, וּשְׁמוּאֵל אָמַר: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יוֹסֵי.",
   "en": "Our mishna continues: «And the she-goats may go out» with their udders «bound.» Rabbi Yosei prohibits doing so. Rabbi Yehuda distinguishes between a case where the udders were bound to dry the milk supply and a case where they were bound to conserve the milk. «It was stated» that the amora’im disagreed with regard to the ruling in this dispute: «Rav said: The halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda, and Shmuel said: The halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yosei.»"
  }
 ],
